A||||17||Alex4mula||Best sources for Caddy 4.9 mounts and carb possible?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||12-11-2001||04:04 PM||||I'm looking for the best sources for 4.5/4.9 Caddy engine mounts for the Fiero. Any other item that needs to be fabricated other than the exhaust?<BR>Also, would it be possible to run these engines with a Holley Street Avanger carb? Any mod to distributor (electronics) required doing this? Would I be able to get rid of the ECM? Any HP benefit with carb? TIA<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||12-11-2001||08:21 PM||||I am sure Bubbajoe has distributor instructions and mounts available.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/bubbajoexx/</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||12-11-2001||08:49 PM||||Is he the only one??<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/vroom_5.gif">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                <BR>      <P> <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||12-11-2001||09:06 PM||||All the info I have needed so far has been found either here. <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.ca/FieroCaddySwapGroup/messageboard.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.ca/FieroCaddySwapGroup/messageboard.msnw</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com/Engine_Swaps/4_9cadswap.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cwestco.com/Engine_Swaps/4_9cadswap.html</A> <P>or posting my questions and Rockcrawl has help to walk us through it.<P>But my main sourse of info has been Bubbajoe, although I am going to run it with the PFI as rockcrawl has.  <p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadero2dmax||12-11-2001||09:15 PM||||Don't forget Ed Parks at the Fiero Factory.<BR>He is putting together a kit for 4.9 installation.<P><P>------------------<BR>Injected 4.9 Cad powered 85 SE (Daily Driver)5 speed ('88 cradle)<P>86 carburated 4.9 automatic Grassroots Motorsports Magazine $2002 Challenge Fiero coupe (2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit) all on an '88 cradle<P>For Racing Photos of my former Q4 Fiero racecar, go to: <BR>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=142520&a=1342821 <P>(until I can figure out how to post photos)<P>George Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000005||PBJ||12-11-2001||09:24 PM||||Does Ed Parks or Fero Factory have a WEB site??||||reg||1
Z||000006||cadero2dmax||12-11-2001||09:28 PM||||Yes, sorta.<P>This is one gentleman every Fiero should get to know. He does 3.4 swaps, 4.9 swaps, or just plain ole stock engines. He has acres of salvaged Fieros, all years, all models. And there are always a number of Fieros for sale.<P>He hosts an annual swap meet, perrenially the last weekend in April every year. Last year there were over 200 in attendance from 30 some odd different states.<P>Give Ed a call, tell him George sent ya.<P>Ed Parks... From: The Fiero Factory<BR>8710B Hwy 53<BR>Toney, Ala 35773<BR>Days: 256-420-5391   Nights 256-882-1568 <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory" TARGET=_blank>http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory</A> <P> <BR><P>------------------<BR>George Ryan<BR>A pair of 4.9 Cadero's<P>For Racing Photos of my former Q4 Fiero racecar, go to: <BR>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=142520&a=1342821 <P>(until I can figure out how to post photos)||||reg||1
Z||000007||PBJ||12-11-2001||09:35 PM||||cadero2dmax -  So you have a pair of 4.9's. How do you run them? ecm wise.<P>Pete||||reg||1
Z||000008||cadero2dmax||12-11-2001||09:48 PM||||My 85 SE is my daily driver, it was built by Greg Duncan of Team Python in Tucson. It has maintained the sequential port injection, with a 5 speed Isuzu tranny.<P>Frankly, I do not know what ECM Greg used,  but it is one of the SBC's because it is totally programmable.<P>The other 4.9 is one in process, I am building it for the Grassroots Motorsports Magazine $2002 Challenge. It will have an early 350 2 bbl Rochester carb and a 2.84:1  FDR TH125 automatic. So instead of an ECM, I need only one 12 volt "hot" wire to the modified Olds distributor.<P>G||||reg||1
Z||000009||Alex4mula||12-12-2001||10:35 AM||||So, is Bubbajoe the only one? I heard of some fit problems with his. Is that true?<BR>Also, what about running a carb? Is that possible? TIA<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||12-12-2001||03:29 PM||||*BUMP* ??<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000011||cadero2dmax||12-12-2001||08:09 PM||||First, let me qualify my comments with the statement I have never seen any of BubbaJoe's parts, only know what others have described.<P>A carb'd 4.9 is a very viable option. An adapter is needed, the one that BubbaJoe sells is supposedly off by a little. I am making my own for the Challenge car. All else that is needed is the distributor, an early Olds 350 distributor with the Cad shaft will work well, and Joe's website chronicles this mod quite well.<P>Also:<P>If you want to run your V8 on mounts that are welded on only one side, buy BubbaJoe. If you want to have to redrill and elongate holes, buy BubbaJoe.<P>If you want to drill holes in your cradle at the motor mounts (what a way to invite a cradle to crack) without a doubler, buy BubbaJoe.<P>If you want to have a quality mount that fits, and won't fail on you, buy from Ed. Or the best option - - as I am doing - - make your own templates, and if you can't weld, take the templates to a welder (as I am doing).<P>Simply set the tranny in it's position on the cradle, the tranny remains in it's stock location. Then take a look at how you want to mount it. I am going with a four corner mount on the engine, and 2 on the tranny because I plan to drive the car in lapping sessions at the track, and occasionally even autocrossing it.<P>Cut cardboard to the shape of the mounts you want to build, tape them together to the exact fit, and take it to a welder. I am having mine made up from 1/4" steel. I also am adding a 1/4" doubler over the mount that bolts directly to the cradle to reinforce the drilled holes.<P>Follow th directions at Rockcrawls site, and "Bingo" - - you are driving a V8 Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>George Ryan<BR>A pair of 4.9 Cadero's<P>For Racing Photos of my former Q4 Fiero racecar, go to:  <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=142520&a=1342821" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumIndex?u=142520&a=1342821</A>  <P>(until I can figure out how to post photos)<P><p>[This message has been edited by cadero2dmax (edited 12-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Alex4mula||12-13-2001||10:57 AM||||Thanks a lot Cadero2dmax. Many people without real experience put this swap as VERY easy but I guess it is not. As soon as you have to fabricate a part then it is not a simple swap like a 3.4, which I have done. I have read everything about this topic here and now joined the Yahoo group because this swap is in my very near future. I started to look for an engine already.<BR>From your explanation it seems that making mounts are not that hard. Maybe better get Eds if they are available as stand-alone now or in next two months.<BR>I'm still confused with the intakes. Is the 89 4.5 TBI the only one you can use with a 4.9? I found a 90 DeVille 4.5 TBI at a yard yesterday and was wondering if I should grab it. What is the difference between 89 and 90? Thanks a lot for sharing your knowledge.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000013||LAMBO||12-13-2001||11:40 AM||||You can make your own mounts without any welding. All you need are two pieces of heavy angle iron (I used 1/4"). Use the stock caddy front mounts and attach them to the angle iron pieces that are bolted to the cradle. I used 4 grade 8 7/16" bolts per mount. A person could then weld these angle pieces to the cradle if he wanted, but I hightly doubt its going anywhere. Mounting the motor to the cradle doesn't require welding, just a drill, very hard bolts, and some careful measuring.<P>TL||||reg||1
Z||000014||Dumba$$||12-13-2001||03:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by cadero2dmax:<BR><B>First, let me qualify my comments with the statement I have never seen any of BubbaJoe's parts, only know what others have described.<P>A carb'd 4.9 is a very viable option. An adapter is needed, the one that BubbaJoe sells is supposedly off by a little. I am making my own for the Challenge car. All else that is needed is the distributor, an early Olds 350 distributor with the Cad shaft will work well, and Joe's website chronicles this mod quite well.<P>Also:<P>If you want to run your V8 on mounts that are welded on only one side, buy BubbaJoe. If you want to have to redrill and elongate holes, buy BubbaJoe.<P>If you want to drill holes in your cradle at the motor mounts (what a way to invite a cradle to crack) without a doubler, buy BubbaJoe.<P>If you want to have a quality mount that fits, and won't fail on you, buy from Ed. Or the best option - - as I am doing - - make your own templates, and if you can't weld, take the templates to a welder (as I am doing).<P>Simply set the tranny in it's position on the cradle, the tranny remains in it's stock location. Then take a look at how you want to mount it. I am going with a four corner mount on the engine, and 2 on the tranny because I plan to drive the car in lapping sessions at the track, and occasionally even autocrossing it.<P>Cut cardboard to the shape of the mounts you want to build, tape them together to the exact fit, and take it to a welder. I am having mine made up from 1/4" steel. I also am adding a 1/4" doubler over the mount that bolts directly to the cradle to reinforce the drilled holes.<P>Follow th directions at Rockcrawls site, and "Bingo" - - you are driving a V8 Fiero.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR> <BR> i have a set of his mounts that im selling with my 4.9 <BR>there $150  they look nice  and seem to be of good Quality ,but there the type of thing that once you have seen in person  thed take a machine shop or a machinst  20 min. to make   ( and probibly charge less than $50 to do for you)<BR> verry simple!!<BR>im not putting him or his product down in any way, im just saying you wouldnt pay $150 twice  if you ever needed a second set you would make them your self!!<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000015||mrfixit58||12-13-2001||03:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex4mula:<BR><B>...I'm still confused with the intakes. Is the 89 4.5 TBI the only one you can use with a 4.9? I found a 90 DeVille 4.5 TBI at a yard yesterday and was wondering if I should grab it. What is the difference between 89 and 90? <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Alex,<P>in 1990, the 4.5 was upgraded to MPI. It had a different intake with larger runners, and the heads had larger valves. The intake also has eight holes above the heads intake port for the fuel injectors. The intake is a duel-plane design. when the motor went to 4.9, the same heads and intake were used.<P>The 89 4.5 is uses the same heads as the earlier 4.1 and has a single plan intake manifold and used a throttle body.<P>If you have the opportunity to get the 4.5 cheap, go for it. There was only about 20 HP difference between the 4.5 and the 4.9. If you going to pay more than about $300, I say look for a 4.9 instead.<P>I think RockCrawl has posted an article on the 4.X motors. This is where I got most of the above information. That, and the 4.5 I took apart in the bone yard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Good luck and keep us posted,<BR>Roy<P>||||reg||10
Z||000016||Alex4mula||12-14-2001||08:20 AM||||Hey Roy, Thanks for the explanation. The 4.5 label confused me. I'll keep looking.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
